    "text": "In Quarta Feria In Letania Maiore Men \u00f0a leofestan, swa cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga lareow, hw\u00e6t we gemunan\n\u00fe\u00e6t wise men \u00feurh Haliges Gastes gyfe gesetton us \u00feas halgan gangdagas \u00fery to f\u00e6stene and on to\nAnd he for ure lufan her on life dea\u00f0 \u00ferowude, and \u00feurh his m\u00e6gen\u00ferymm he eft on \u00e6rest aras and his\nAnd hi myngode \u00fe\u00e6re gastlican lare \u00fee he him \u00e6r his \u00ferowunga s\u00e6de.\nAnd \u00fereo and \u00ferittig wintra on \u00feyssum middanearde he w\u00e6s and \u00e6ghwilces godes bysene he us\nFor\u00f0an we sceolan biddan hine for his \u00fe\u00e6re halgan rode weor\u00feunge and his upstige to heofonum.\nAnd ealle his halegan we sceolon eac biddan, \u00fe\u00e6t hi mid us bidden \u00e6lmihtigne Drihten, \u00feone ecan\nAnd uton we hine eac biddan \u00fe\u00e6t he us gescylde wi\u00f0 grimnysse myssenlicra yfela and wita \u00feara \u00fee he\nTo \u00feyssum dagum \u00feurh Haligne Gast \u00feys f\u00e6sten and \u00fees gang geseted w\u00e6s.\nSwa we oft on bocum gehyrdon secgan \u00fe\u00e6t we mid \u00fe\u00e6re halegan \u00derynnysse rode and mid his halegra\nUton we nu hine georne biddan, nu he us forgeaf \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00feisse tide gebidan moston, \u00fe\u00e6t he his yrre\nMen \u00f0a leofestan, gehyra\u00f0 lifes bebodu and \u00fea ecan lare lustlice onfo\u00f0 and ongyta\u00f0 \u00feone cwyde \u00fe\u00e6s\nFor\u00f0an Drihten \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, Se \u00f0e forhig\u00f0 \u00feone lareow, ondr\u00e6de he him \u00feone heofonlican Deman \u00fe\u00e6t is\nHys leorneras w\u00e6ron lareowas genemnede for\u00f0an hi us \u00fea halgan lare of Godes bocum secga\u00f0 and \u00fe\u00e6s\nFor\u00f0an \u00f0e he cym\u00f0 to demenne eallum middanearde, for\u00f0an \u00feone so\u00f0an Deman urne Drihten we us\nWarnien we us \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee he cume, and tiligen we georne \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00feonne gemette syn on godum d\u00e6dum;\n\u00fe\u00e6t ys yrm\u00f0e d\u00e6g and gnornunge d\u00e6g and unrotnysse d\u00e6g and wanunge d\u00e6g and nearonysse d\u00e6g and\n\u00de\u00e6t is gewryxles d\u00e6g lichamana and sawla and ne by\u00f0 n\u00e6nig m\u00e6g\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s micclan mancynnes\nNe snytero ne gleawnys ne n\u00e6nig man nah swa micel rice on \u00feysum middanearde \u00fe\u00e6t he hine \u00fe\u00e6r\n\u00d0\u00e6t is cy\u00f0nysse d\u00e6g mancynnes \u00feurh gesceafte fyres and w\u00e6teres and windes and \u00feunurada swi\u00f0e\n\u00de\u00e6t ys byman d\u00e6g and hire hleo\u00f0runga. \u00feisne d\u00e6g we us on micelre hrernysse toweardne ongytan\nBe \u00feam d\u00e6ge Drihten sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t arisa\u00f0 \u00feeoda wi\u00f0 \u00feeode and rice wi\u00f0 ricum.\n\u00feonne bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r \u00feeoda ge\u00fering and m\u00e6nigfeald hreownys geond m\u00e6nige stowa.\n\u00feas eor\u00f0lican tacnu we nu gewordene oft sceawia\u00f0. \u00feonne gewur\u00fea\u00f0 \u00feas tacnu seofon dagum \u00e6r \u00feam\nOn \u00f0am \u00e6restan domesd\u00e6ges tacne by\u00f0 micel stefen gehyred of \u00feam heofones tungle se hatte\nOn \u00feam \u00e6fteran d\u00e6ge stefen by\u00f0 gehyred of heofonum and eor\u00f0e by\u00f0 onhrered and heofoncund leoht\nOn \u00feam \u00feriddan d\u00e6ge \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re \u00e6fteran tide d\u00e6ges on heofonum \u00e6teowe\u00f0 fyrentacen and of eor\u00f0an\nAnd \u00e6t \u00feam feower healfum \u00feyses middaneardes se heofon tobyrste\u00f0 and micel sweg cym\u00f0 and\nAnd of helle astih\u00fe dimnysse and fulnysse stenc and oferh\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00feas eor\u00f0an ane tid d\u00e6ges.\n\u00deonne ongyta\u00f0 synfulle men hyra forwyrd and forwyrhtu.\nOn \u00f0am feor\u00f0an d\u00e6ge fram nor\u00f0d\u00e6le middaneardes micel hream astih\u00fe hellegasta.\n\u00deonne fyl\u00f0 eall h\u00e6\u00feenra manna deofolgyld on \u00feam d\u00e6ge.\nOn \u00feam fiftan d\u00e6ge \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re fiftan tide d\u00e6ges samnunga cuma\u00f0 \u00feunerada swi\u00f0e micele and storm\n\u00deonne ealle \u00feeoda wi\u00f0saca\u00f0 \u00feisse worulde and hi ongyta\u00f0 Drihtnes mihte.\nOn \u00feam sixtan d\u00e6ge \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re sixtan tide d\u00e6ges \u00fees heofon tohlit fram eastd\u00e6le o\u00f0 \u00f0one westd\u00e6l and\n\u00deonne \u00fea arleasan men fleo\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t heofoncunde werud hi sylfe to behydenne on dunum and on beorgum\nOn \u00feam seofo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re seofo\u00f0an tide d\u00e6ges by\u00f0 domesd\u00e6ges tacn and \u00e6t \u00feam feower healfum\n\u00deonne befealt \u00fees heofon tog\u00e6dere swa man boc betyne and seo sunne by\u00f0 onwended on \u00feeostru and se\nDrihten cym\u00f0 \u00feonne on micclum m\u00e6gen\u00ferymme and fyr on his onsyne scin\u00f0 and on his ymbhwyrfte\n\u00deonne arisa\u00f0 ealle \u00fea men, \u00fea \u00f0e mid gebregednyssum on dea\u00f0e swulton, fram \u00feam feower healfum\nEalle \u00fea \u00feonne \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re byman stefne arisa\u00f0 and \u00feurh fyres leoman to Godes dome ga\u00f0.\n\u00de\u00e6r \u00e6tstanda\u00f0 \u00feusend \u00feusend engla and micel m\u00e6gen heahengla and ealle halige and so\u00f0f\u00e6ste Godes\n\u00deonne \u00e6tywe\u00f0 Drihten \u00fea rode \u00fee he on \u00ferowode and \u00fe\u00e6r scine\u00f0 leoht ofer ealne middaneard, and he\n\u00deonne cwy\u00f0 se eca Cyning to anre gehwylcum, Men \u00f0a leofestan, sege me hw\u00e6t ge\u00feohtest \u00feu o\u00f0\u00f0e\nSyle wed be \u00feysum eallum \u00fee ic for \u00f0e dyde and for \u00f0e \u00ferowude.\n\u00deonne andswara\u00f0 se man urum Drihtne and cwy\u00f0, N\u00e6bbe ic \u00e6nig wedd to syllenne buton mine sawle.\n\u00deonne by\u00f0 sum boc untyned on ansyne \u00fe\u00e6s hehstan Cyninges.\nOn \u00f0\u00e6re beo\u00f0 awritene \u00e6ghwilces mannes d\u00e6da, eal \u00fe\u00e6t he to gode o\u00f0\u00f0e to yfele gedyde on \u00feysum\n\u00de\u00e6r se bro\u00f0or ne m\u00e6g \u00feam o\u00f0rum helpan ne se f\u00e6der \u00feam suna, ne \u00fea neahmagas ne \u00f0a ma\u00f0mgestreon\nAc Drihten gylde\u00f0 anra gehwylcum menn \u00e6fter his sylfes gewyrhtum.\n\u00feonne so\u00f0f\u00e6ste and gecorene men for\u00f0b\u00e6ra\u00f0 heora wurca hyrsumnysse and Drihtnes halige martyras\nMunecas b\u00e6ra\u00f0 heora hyrsumnysse and forwyrnednysse \u00feyssa woruldlicra \u00feinga and heora \u00fea\nL\u00e6wede men, \u00fea \u00f0e her on worulde rihtlice heora lif libba\u00f0, hi b\u00e6ra\u00f0 heora \u00e6lmysd\u00e6da and hluttor lif\n\u00deonne \u00fea arleasan and \u00fea synfullan hi b\u00e6ra\u00f0 nearowne w\u00e6stm and sceand fulne on ansyne \u00fe\u00e6s\nAnd hi \u00feonne ahwyrfa\u00f0 fram haligra manna dreame and swi\u00f0e heofigende hellewitu seca\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6r is\n\u00de\u00e6r ne ongyt se f\u00e6der \u00feone sunu ne se sunu \u00feone f\u00e6der ne wyr\u00f0a\u00f0, ne seo dohtor \u00fea modor ne lufa\u00f0\nac anra gehwilc hys sylfes yrm\u00f0a wepa\u00f0 and heofa\u00f0; for\u00f0an \u00f0e hellefyr n\u00e6fre ne by\u00f0 adw\u00e6sced ac \u00fea\n\u00fe\u00e6r is eagena wop and to\u00f0a gristbitung and \u00fe\u00e6r is welera \u00feurst and wita stow.\nOf \u00feysum tintregum, men \u00f0a leofestan, tiligen we us to gescildenne and us to gewarnigenne \u00fea hwile\nAnd mid geornfullum mode tiligen we ure sylfra, swa lange swa we lybbon on \u00feysum life mid godum\n\u00de\u00e6r is ece blis and engla sang ungeswy\u00f0rod and unasecgendlic gefea and Godes lof and unawendedlic\nSwa us cydde Sanctus Iohannes, se Drihtnes dyrling, se sceawode heofona rices wuldor.\nAnd he on heofonum w\u00e6s and he cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic geseo niwne heofon and niwe eor\u00f0an and \u00fea halgan\nAnd heo w\u00e6s befangen mid swi\u00f0e micclon wealle and tw\u00e6lf gatu w\u00e6ron on \u00fe\u00e6re ceastre \u00fea w\u00e6ron\nAnd seo ceaster w\u00e6s ymbseald mid Godes beorhtnysse and hire sta\u00f0ol w\u00e6s of eallum deorwur\u00f0um\nAnd on \u00f0\u00e6re ceastre sunne ne lihte\u00f0 ne mona ac Godes beorhtnys hi onlihte\u00f0 and seo beorhtnys w\u00e6s\n\u00de\u00e6r ineodon ealle \u00feeoda and eor\u00f0cyningas; hi comon and gesawon Godes wuldor and his m\u00e6gen\u00ferym\nAnd \u00e6fter \u00fean cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sanctus Iohannes, Ic geseah micele men gangan of eallum \u00feeodum.\n\u00dea w\u00e6ron beswapene ealle mid hwitum hr\u00e6glum and clypedon and cw\u00e6don, Si h\u00e6lo urum Drihtne\nFor\u00f0on us is micel neod\u00feearf, men \u00f0a leofestan, \u00fe\u00e6t we biddan \u00fea heofoncundan gesamnunga \u00fe\u00e6t hi\nAnd Sanctus Michael \u00feone heahengel utan we us on fultum cygen, se ys hyrde neorxnawanges and\nHe geweald h\u00e6f\u00f0, and he n\u00e6fre hi forl\u00e6t \u00e6r he hi gebringe beforan Drihtnes hehsetle, \u00fe\u00e6r is\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00fe\u00e6t hea rice and \u00fe\u00e6t herigendlice and \u00fe\u00e6t smylte and \u00fe\u00e6t gesibsume \u00fe\u00e6t God his haligum\nMen \u00f0a leofestan, herien we nu \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan Drihten and lufien we hine and wur\u00f0igen.\nHe is Cyning ealra cyninga and he ys Scyppend ealra gesceafta gesewenlicra and ungesewenlicra.\nAnd he is f\u00e6grost ealra blostma and he is snytro \u00fe\u00e6re so\u00f0an lufe.\nHe ys engla symbelnys and he is wuldor \u00fe\u00e6ra eadigra apostola and he is leoht \u00fe\u00e6ra haligra martyra.\nAnd he is neorxnawanges ece gefea and he is h\u00e6lo ealra untrumra and he is alysend \u00fe\u00e6ra geh\u00e6ftendra\nBidden we nu, men \u00f0a leofestan urne Drihten, wuldres Cyning, \u00fe\u00e6t he us gehwyrfe to his willan and\nHe is Drihten sylfa se \u00f0e leofa\u00f0 and rixa\u00f0 mid Suna and mid \u00feam Halgan Gaste a buton ende. amen.",
